PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L01U5.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":1,"cefr":"A1a","unit":5,"theme":"My Home","essential_question":"What makes a house a home?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS1","title":"There Is a Garden: there is / there are","objectives":["Students will be able to use there is with one thing and there are with many things.","Students will be able to describe rooms in a house with there is/there are.","I can say \"There is a sofa\" and \"There are two beds\".","I can describe my home."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام there is مع المفرد وthere are مع الجمع.","سيتمكن الطلاب من وصف غرف البيت باستخدام there is وthere are.","أستطيع أن أقول There is a sofa وThere are two beds.","أستطيع أن أصف بيتي."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"house","pos":"noun","ipa":"/haʊs/","definition":"a building where a family lives","arabic":"بيت / منزل","example":"Our house has a blue door.","image_id":"GV-L01-U5-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS1-W01"},{"word":"kitchen","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkɪtʃən/","definition":"the room where we cook food","arabic":"مطبخ","example":"Mom is making tea in the kitchen.","image_id":"GV-L01-U5-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS1-W02"},{"word":"bedroom","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbɛˌdrum/","definition":"the room where we sleep","arabic":"غرفة نوم","example":"My bedroom has a big window.","image_id":"GV-L01-U5-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS1-W03"},{"word":"bathroom","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbæˌθrum/","definition":"the room where we wash","arabic":"دورة المياه / الحمّام","example":"The bathroom is next to my room.","image_id":"GV-L01-U5-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"We use there is and there are to say that something exists in a place.\nUse there is (there's) with one thing: There is a lamp. Use there are with two or more things: There are two lamps.\nThere is + a/an + singular noun: There is a rug.\nThere are + plural noun: There are three bedrooms.\nShort form: there's = there is. (We don't shorten \"there are\" in writing.)","examples":["There is a lamp on my desk.","There are two bathrooms in our house.","There's a cat in the garden!","There are many plants on the balcony.","There isn't a sofa in the kitchen.","Is there a park near your house?","Are there any apples in the fridge?","There are five rooms on the first floor."],"common_errors":["✗ In my house have a garden. → ✓ There is a garden in my house. (Arabic says في بيتي حديقة; English uses there is.)","✗ There is two bedrooms. → ✓ There are two bedrooms. (Two or more → there are.)","✗ There are a sofa. → ✓ There is a sofa. (One thing → there is.)"],"arabic":"نستخدم there is مع المفرد وthere are مع الجمع لنقول إن شيئًا موجود في مكان ما.\nفي العربية نقول «في غرفتي سرير»، وفي الإنجليزية نقول: There is a bed in my room.\nلا نستخدم have لهذا المعنى: There is a garden وليس In my house have a garden."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “There Is a Garden: there is / there are”. Let’s learn there is / there are together.","on_screen":"GV-L01-U5-LS1 | There Is a Garden: there is / there are","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “Welcome to My Home”: Hello! I'm Noura. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"Hello! I'm Noura.","visual":"Image GV-L01-U5-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"We use there is and there are to say that something exists in a place. Use there is (there's) with one thing: There is a lamp. Use there are with two or more things: There are two lamps.","on_screen":"There is + a/an + singular noun: There is a rug. • There are + plural noun: There are three bedrooms. • Short form: there's = there is. (We don't shorten \"there are\" in writing.)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. There is a lamp on my desk. There are two bathrooms in our house. There's a cat in the garden!","on_screen":"There is a lamp on my desk. / There are two bathrooms in our house. / There's a cat in the garden!","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “In my house have a garden.” That’s not right. We say: “There is a garden in my house.”","on_screen":"✗ In my house have a garden.   ✓ There is a garden in my house.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"There ___ two lamps.\" One lamp or more? is or are? … Think! … More than one – *are*. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"There is a sofa\" and \"There are two beds\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"There is a sofa\" and \"There are two beds\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: there is / there are.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نستخدم there is مع المفرد وthere are مع الجمع لنقول إن شيئًا موجود في مكان ما.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: In my house have a garden. — الصحيح: There is a garden in my house.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول There is a sofa وThere are two beds."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Welcome to My Home","body":"Hello! I'm Noura. Welcome to my home!\nThere is a big living room. There are two sofas and a red rug in it.\nThere is a kitchen next to the living room.\nThere are three bedrooms upstairs.\nIn my bedroom, there is a bed, a desk and a lamp.\nThere are many books on my bookcase.\nBehind the house, there is a garden with palm trees.\nI love my home!","word_count":70,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"___ a sofa in the living room.","options":["It have","Is there","There is","There are"],"answer":"There is","explanation":"One thing → there is.","explanation_ar":"للمفرد نستخدم there is."},{"q":"___ three windows in my room.","options":["There is","It has","There's","There are"],"answer":"There are","explanation":"Two or more things → there are.","explanation_ar":"للجمع نستخدم there are."},{"q":"There ___ a lamp next to my bed.","options":["is","am","are","have"],"answer":"is","explanation":"One thing → there is.","explanation_ar":"للمفرد نستخدم there is."},{"q":"There ___ two cats in the garden.","options":["is","are","am","has"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Two or more things → there are.","explanation_ar":"للجمع نستخدم there are."},{"q":"___ a big kitchen in Grandma's house.","options":["It are","There are","In it have","There is"],"answer":"There is","explanation":"Use there is/are, not have, to say something is in a place.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم there is وليس have."},{"q":"There ___ many books on the bookcase.","options":["is","are","has","am"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Two or more things → there are.","explanation_ar":"للجمع نستخدم there are."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS1-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write is or are. Word bank: is, are","items":[{"q":"There ______ a mirror in the bathroom.","options":[],"answer":"is","explanation":"One thing → there is.","explanation_ar":"للمفرد نستخدم there is."},{"q":"There ______ six chairs in the kitchen.","options":[],"answer":"are","explanation":"Two or more things → there are.","explanation_ar":"للجمع نستخدم there are."},{"q":"There ______ an old clock in the hall.","options":[],"answer":"is","explanation":"One thing → there is.","explanation_ar":"للمفرد نستخدم there is."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS1-B2","type":"order","instructions":"Guided practice: Put the words in order.","items":[{"q":"are / bedrooms / There / two   ( . )","options":["are","bedrooms","There","two"],"answer":"There are two bedrooms.","explanation":"Word order: Two or more things → there are.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الكلمات: للجمع نستخدم there are."},{"q":"There / floor / the / on / is / rug / a   ( . )","options":["There","floor","the","on","is","rug","a"],"answer":"There is a rug on the floor.","explanation":"Word order: One thing → there is.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الكلمات: للمفرد نستخدم there is."},{"q":"There / are / garden / palm trees / in / the   ( . )","options":["There","are","garden","palm trees","in","the"],"answer":"There are palm trees in the garden.","explanation":"Word order: Two or more things → there are.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الكلمات: للجمع نستخدم there are."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write about your home.","items":[{"q":"In my bedroom, there is ___.","options":[],"answer":"In my bedroom, there is a bed.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses there is / there are correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"In my kitchen, there are ___.","options":[],"answer":"In my kitchen, there are four chairs.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses there is / there are correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"In my living room, there is a ___ and a ___.","options":[],"answer":"In my living room, there is a sofa and a TV.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses there is / there are correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"In my house, there are ___ bedrooms.","options":[],"answer":"In my house, there are three bedrooms.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses there is / there are correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Outside my house, there is ___.","options":[],"answer":"Outside my house, there is a small garden.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses there is / there are correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Draw and describe.","items":[{"q":"Draw your bedroom. Write 3 sentences with there is or there are.","options":[],"answer":"There is a bed. There is a lamp. There are two pictures on the wall.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses there is / there are correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences about your dream house.","options":[],"answer":"There is a big pool. There are ten bedrooms.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses there is / there are correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Tell your partner about your kitchen. Write 2 of his sentences.","options":[],"answer":"There is a big fridge. There are three cups on the table.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses there is / there are correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Ball Toss Sentences","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["Students stand in a circle. The teacher says a cue word and throws the ball.","The catcher makes a sentence with the cue word and there is / there are.","If it is correct, the catcher chooses the next cue word and throws the ball to a new student.","If it is not correct, classmates help fix it, and the same student tries again."],"data":[{"label":"a sofa"},{"label":"two beds"},{"label":"a lamp"},{"label":"three chairs"},{"label":"a garden"},{"label":"many books"},{"label":"a rug"},{"label":"an oven"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"___ a garden behind my house.","options":["Is there","It have","There are","There is"],"answer":"There is","explanation":"One thing → there is.","explanation_ar":"للمفرد نستخدم there is."},{"q":"There ___ four rooms upstairs.","options":["am","has","is","are"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Two or more things → there are.","explanation_ar":"للجمع نستخدم there are."},{"q":"There ___ a TV in the living room.","options":["have","is","am","are"],"answer":"is","explanation":"One thing → there is.","explanation_ar":"للمفرد نستخدم there is."},{"q":"","options":["It have two bathrooms.","There is two bathrooms.","There are two bathrooms.","There are two bathroom."],"answer":"There are two bathrooms.","explanation":"Two or more things → there are.","explanation_ar":"للجمع نستخدم there are."},{"q":"There ___ many plants on the balcony.","options":["are","am","is","be"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Two or more things → there are.","explanation_ar":"للجمع نستخدم there are."},{"q":"","options":["There is a bed in my room.","In my room have a bed.","There are a bed in my room.","There is bed in my room."],"answer":"There is a bed in my room.","explanation":"Use there is/are, not have, to say something is in a place.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم there is وليس have."},{"q":"There's ___ in the kitchen.","options":["two ovens","many ovens","an oven","ovens"],"answer":"an oven","explanation":"One thing → there is.","explanation_ar":"للمفرد نستخدم there is."},{"q":"There are ___ in the garden.","options":["three trees","a tree","tree","an tree"],"answer":"three trees","explanation":"Two or more things → there are.","explanation_ar":"للجمع نستخدم there are."},{"q":"","options":["There are a rug in the hall.","There is a rug in the hall.","There is rug in the hall.","It is have a rug in the hall."],"answer":"There is a rug in the hall.","explanation":"One thing → there is.","explanation_ar":"للمفرد نستخدم there is."},{"q":"___ two sofas in our living room.","options":["It has","There's","There is","There are"],"answer":"There are","explanation":"Two or more things → there are.","explanation_ar":"للجمع نستخدم there are."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"Noura giving a tour of her home: a living room with two sofas and a rug, a kitchen through a door, stairs going up and a garden with palm trees seen through the window. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Noura giving a tour of her home: a living room with two sofas and a rug, a kitchen through a door, stairs going up and a garden with palm trees seen through the window"},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about there is / there are, with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about there is / there are, with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right"},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows house (a building where a family lives); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing house: a building where a family lives"},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows kitchen (the room where we cook food); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing kitchen: the room where we cook food"},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows bedroom (the room where we sleep); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing bedroom: the room where we sleep"},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows bathroom (the room where we wash); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing bathroom: the room where we wash"},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Ball Toss Sentences”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Ball Toss Sentences"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS1-W01","script":"house. house. Our house has a blue door.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS1-W02","script":"kitchen. kitchen. Mom is making tea in the kitchen.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS1-W03","script":"bedroom. bedroom. My bedroom has a big window.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS1-W04","script":"bathroom. bathroom. The bathroom is next to my room.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS1-T1","script":"Hello! I'm Noura. Welcome to my home! There is a big living room. There are two sofas and a red rug in it. There is a kitchen next to the living room. There are three bedrooms upstairs. In my bedroom, there is a bed, a desk and a lamp. There are many books on my bookcase. Behind the house, there is a garden with palm trees. I love my home!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “There Is a Garden: there is / there are”. Let’s learn there is / there are together. Listen to the start of “Welcome to My Home”: Hello! I'm Noura. Look at the green words. We use there is and there are to say that something exists in a place. Use there is (there's) with one thing: There is a lamp. Use there are with two or more things: There are two lamps. Here are some examples. There is a lamp on my desk. There are two bathrooms in our house. There's a cat in the garden! Be careful! Some learners say: “In my house have a garden.” That’s not right. We say: “There is a garden in my house.” Quick check: \"There ___ two lamps.\" One lamp or more? is or are? … Think! … More than one – *are*. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"There is a sofa\" and \"There are two beds\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS2","title":"Where Is the Cat? Prepositions of Place","objectives":["Students will be able to say where things are with in, on, under, next to, behind and in front of.","Students will be able to ask and answer Is there…? and Are there…? questions.","I can say \"The cat is under the bed\".","I can ask \"Is there a lamp in your room?\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تحديد أماكن الأشياء باستخدام in وon وunder وnext to وbehind وin front of.","سيتمكن الطلاب من طرح أسئلة Is there…? وAre there…? والإجابة عنها.","أستطيع أن أقول The cat is under the bed.","أستطيع أن أسأل Is there a lamp in your room?"],"vocabulary":[{"word":"living room","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈlɪvɪŋ rum/","definition":"the room where the family sits and talks","arabic":"غرفة المعيشة","example":"We watch the news in the living room.","image_id":"GV-L01-U5-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS2-W01"},{"word":"garden","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɡɑrdən/","definition":"the land outside a house with plants and flowers","arabic":"حديقة","example":"Grandpa waters the garden every evening.","image_id":"GV-L01-U5-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS2-W02"},{"word":"sofa","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsoʊfə/","definition":"a long soft seat for two or more people","arabic":"أريكة / كنبة","example":"The cat is asleep on the sofa.","image_id":"GV-L01-U5-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS2-W03"},{"word":"bed","pos":"noun","ipa":"/bɛd/","definition":"the thing you sleep on","arabic":"سرير","example":"Make your bed in the morning.","image_id":"GV-L01-U5-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Prepositions of place tell us where something is: The cat is under the bed.\nin = inside; on = touching the top; under = below; next to = beside; behind = at the back; in front of = before.\nAsk with Is there…? (one) and Are there…? (many). Use any in questions and negatives with plurals: Are there any cups?","examples":["My shoes are under the bed.","The poster is on the bedroom door.","The car is in front of the house.","There's a small garden behind our building.","The lamp is next to the sofa.","The milk is in the fridge.","Is there a mirror in the bathroom? – Yes, there is.","Are there any pencils on the desk? – No, there aren't."],"common_errors":["✗ The picture is in the wall. → ✓ The picture is on the wall. (Things touching a surface are on it.)","✗ The car is in front the house. → ✓ The car is in front of the house. (Don't forget of.)","✗ There is a cat under the bed? → ✓ Is there a cat under the bed? (In questions, is comes first.)"],"arabic":"in = في (داخل)، on = على، under = تحت، next to = بجانب، behind = خلف، in front of = أمام.\nالصورة على الحائط: The picture is on the wall (وليس in).\nللسؤال نقدّم is أو are: Is there a lamp? / Are there any books?"},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Where Is the Cat? Prepositions of Place”. Let’s learn prepositions of place (in, on, under, next to, behind, in front of) + Is there…? / Are there…? together.","on_screen":"GV-L01-U5-LS2 | Where Is the Cat? Prepositions of Place","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: The ball is on the shelf. • There are shoes next to the door. The cat isn't in the box. • There aren't any chairs in the hall. Is there a lamp in your room? – Yes, there is. • Are there any books under the bed? – No, there aren't. • Where is the cat? – It's under the bed.","on_screen":"The ball is on the shelf. • There are shoes next to the door. | The cat isn't in the box. • There aren't any chairs in the hall. | Is there a lamp in your room? – Yes, there is. • Are there any books under the bed? – No, there aren't. • Where is the cat? – It's under the bed.","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Prepositions of place tell us where something is: The cat is under the bed. in = inside; on = touching the top; under = below; next to = beside; behind = at the back; in front of = before.","on_screen":"prepositions of place (in, on, under, next to, behind, in front of) + Is there…? / Are there…?","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. My shoes are under the bed. The poster is on the bedroom door. The car is in front of the house.","on_screen":"My shoes are under the bed. / The poster is on the bedroom door. / The car is in front of the house.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “The picture is in the wall.” That’s not right. We say: “The picture is on the wall.” Things touching a surface are on it.","on_screen":"✗ The picture is in the wall.   ✓ The picture is on the wall.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: The book is touching the top of the table. in or on? … Think! … *on* Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"The cat is under the bed\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"The cat is under the bed\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: prepositions of place (in, on, under, next to, behind, in front of) + Is there…? / Are there…?.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","in = في (داخل)، on = على، under = تحت، next to = بجانب، behind = خلف، in front of = أمام.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: The picture is in the wall. — الصحيح: The picture is on the wall.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول The cat is under the bed."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Look at the picture of Omar's room. Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"The cat is ___ the bed.","options":["in","on","behind","under"],"answer":"under","explanation":"under = below something.","explanation_ar":"under تعني تحت."},{"q":"The ball is ___ the shelf.","options":["in front","on","under","next"],"answer":"on","explanation":"on = touching the top or a surface (a wall, a table).","explanation_ar":"on تعني على السطح."},{"q":"The shoes are ___ the door.","options":["on to","in front","next","next to"],"answer":"next to","explanation":"next to = beside.","explanation_ar":"next to تعني بجانب."},{"q":"The bag is ___ the chair.","options":["between of","in front","behind","on to"],"answer":"behind","explanation":"behind = at the back of.","explanation_ar":"behind تعني خلف."},{"q":"The pencils are ___ the box.","options":["in","under","of","on"],"answer":"in","explanation":"in = inside something.","explanation_ar":"in تعني داخل."},{"q":"___ any books under the bed?","options":["Are there","Is there","There is","There are"],"answer":"Are there","explanation":"Questions: Is there (one) / Are there any (many).","explanation_ar":"السؤال: Is there للمفرد وAre there any للجمع."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS2-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write the preposition. Word bank: in, on, in front of","items":[{"q":"Put the milk ______ the fridge, please.","options":[],"answer":"in","explanation":"in = inside something.","explanation_ar":"in تعني داخل."},{"q":"The family photo is ______ the wall.","options":[],"answer":"on","explanation":"on = touching the top or a surface (a wall, a table).","explanation_ar":"on تعني على السطح."},{"q":"The car is ______ the garage.","options":[],"answer":"in front of","explanation":"in front of = before; don't forget of.","explanation_ar":"in front of تعني أمام."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS2-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Make a question with Is there or Are there.","items":[{"q":"There is a TV in the bedroom.  (question)","options":[],"answer":"Is there a TV in the bedroom?","explanation":"Questions: Is there (one) / Are there any (many).","explanation_ar":"السؤال: Is there للمفرد وAre there any للجمع."},{"q":"There are some cups on the table.  (question)","options":[],"answer":"Are there any cups on the table?","explanation":"Questions: Is there (one) / Are there any (many).","explanation_ar":"السؤال: Is there للمفرد وAre there any للجمع."},{"q":"There is a park near your house.  (question)","options":[],"answer":"Is there a park near your house?","explanation":"Questions: Is there (one) / Are there any (many).","explanation_ar":"السؤال: Is there للمفرد وAre there any للجمع."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Answer about your home.","items":[{"q":"Where is your bed?","options":[],"answer":"My bed is next to the window.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses prepositions of place (in, on, under, next to, behind, in front of) + Is there…? / Are there…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What is on your desk?","options":[],"answer":"There is a lamp on my desk.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses prepositions of place (in, on, under, next to, behind, in front of) + Is there…? / Are there…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Is there a garden behind your house?","options":[],"answer":"No, there isn't.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses prepositions of place (in, on, under, next to, behind, in front of) + Is there…? / Are there…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Are there any pictures on your bedroom wall?","options":[],"answer":"Yes, there are.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses prepositions of place (in, on, under, next to, behind, in front of) + Is there…? / Are there…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What is under your bed?","options":[],"answer":"My shoes are under my bed.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses prepositions of place (in, on, under, next to, behind, in front of) + Is there…? / Are there…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Play \"Hide and Find\".","items":[{"q":"Hide a toy in a picture of a room. Write 3 clues with prepositions.","options":[],"answer":"It isn't on the sofa. It is behind the lamp. It is next to the bookcase.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses prepositions of place (in, on, under, next to, behind, in front of) + Is there…? / Are there…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 questions to find your partner's hidden toy.","options":[],"answer":"Is it under the bed? Is it in the box? Is it behind the door?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses prepositions of place (in, on, under, next to, behind, in front of) + Is there…? / Are there…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Draw your partner's bedroom from his description. Write 2 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"His bed is next to the door. There is a rug on the floor.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses prepositions of place (in, on, under, next to, behind, in front of) + Is there…? / Are there…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Dice Sentences","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["Turn over a cue card and roll the die.","Make a sentence with the cue in the form shown by the die.","The player on the left checks; a correct sentence wins the card.","The player with the most cards after 7 minutes wins."],"data":[{"cue":"a cat / under / the table"},{"cue":"the lamp / on / the desk"},{"cue":"my shoes / next to / the door"},{"cue":"a garden / behind / the house"},{"cue":"the car / in front of / the house"},{"cue":"the books / in / the bookcase"},{"cue":"the rug / under / the sofa"},{"cue":"a clock / on / the wall"},{"cue":"the bike / behind / the door"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"The keys are ___ the table. (on top)","options":["on","in","of","under"],"answer":"on","explanation":"on = touching the top or a surface (a wall, a table).","explanation_ar":"on تعني على السطح."},{"q":"The dog is ___ its house. (inside)","options":["under","on","next","in"],"answer":"in","explanation":"in = inside something.","explanation_ar":"in تعني داخل."},{"q":"The bike is ___ the tree. (at the back)","options":["in of","behind","on","in front"],"answer":"behind","explanation":"behind = at the back of.","explanation_ar":"behind تعني خلف."},{"q":"","options":["The lamp is next of the sofa.","The lamp next to is the sofa.","The lamp is next to the sofa.","The lamp is next the sofa."],"answer":"The lamp is next to the sofa.","explanation":"next to = beside.","explanation_ar":"next to تعني بجانب."},{"q":"","options":["The bus stops in front of the school.","The bus stops in front the school.","The bus stops front of the school.","The bus stops in the front school."],"answer":"The bus stops in front of the school.","explanation":"in front of = before; don't forget of.","explanation_ar":"in front of تعني أمام."},{"q":"The cat is ___ the table. (below it)","options":["on","above of","under","in"],"answer":"under","explanation":"under = below something.","explanation_ar":"under تعني تحت."},{"q":"___ a mirror in your bathroom? – Yes, there is.","options":["There is","Are there","Is there","Have"],"answer":"Is there","explanation":"Questions: Is there (one) / Are there any (many).","explanation_ar":"السؤال: Is there للمفرد وAre there any للجمع."},{"q":"","options":["Are there any eggs in the fridge?","Is there any eggs in the fridge?","Are there an eggs in the fridge?","There are any eggs in the fridge?"],"answer":"Are there any eggs in the fridge?","explanation":"Questions: Is there (one) / Are there any (many).","explanation_ar":"السؤال: Is there للمفرد وAre there any للجمع."},{"q":"The calendar is ___ the wall.","options":["at","on","in","under"],"answer":"on","explanation":"on = touching the top or a surface (a wall, a table).","explanation_ar":"on تعني على السطح."},{"q":"Where is your bag? – ___","options":["It under my desk.","There under my desk.","Is under my desk.","It's under my desk."],"answer":"It's under my desk.","explanation":"under = below something.","explanation_ar":"under تعني تحت."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"A cozy bedroom where a striped cat hides under the bed, a ball is on the shelf, shoes are next to the door and a bag is behind the chair; Omar searching with a puzzled face. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A cozy bedroom where a striped cat hides under the bed, a ball is on the shelf, shoes are next to the door and a bag is behind the chair; Omar searching with a puzzled face"},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of prepositions of place (in, on, under, next to, behind, in front of) + Is there…? / Are there…?: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “My Home”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of prepositions of place (in, on, under, next to, behind, in front of) + Is there…? / Are there…?: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “My Home”"},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows living room (the room where the family sits and talks); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing living room: the room where the family sits and talks"},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows garden (the land outside a house with plants and flowers); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing garden: the land outside a house with plants and flowers"},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows sofa (a long soft seat for two or more people); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing sofa: a long soft seat for two or more people"},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows bed (the thing you sleep on); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing bed: the thing you sleep on"},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Dice Sentences”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Dice Sentences"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS2-W01","script":"living room. living room. We watch the news in the living room.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS2-W02","script":"garden. garden. Grandpa waters the garden every evening.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS2-W03","script":"sofa. sofa. The cat is asleep on the sofa.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS2-W04","script":"bed. bed. Make your bed in the morning.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Where Is the Cat? Prepositions of Place”. Let’s learn prepositions of place (in, on, under, next to, behind, in front of) + Is there…? / Are there…? together. Remember these patterns: The ball is on the shelf. • There are shoes next to the door. The cat isn't in the box. • There aren't any chairs in the hall. Is there a lamp in your room? – Yes, there is. • Are there any books under the bed? – No, there aren't. • Where is the cat? – It's under the bed. Prepositions of place tell us where something is: The cat is under the bed. in = inside; on = touching the top; under = below; next to = beside; behind = at the back; in front of = before. Here are some examples. My shoes are under the bed. The poster is on the bedroom door. The car is in front of the house. Be careful! Some learners say: “The picture is in the wall.” That’s not right. We say: “The picture is on the wall.” Things touching a surface are on it. Quick check: The book is touching the top of the table. in or on? … Think! … *on* Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"The cat is under the bed\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS3","title":"Rooms and Furniture: Compound Words","objectives":["Students will be able to name rooms and furniture in a house.","Students will be able to build and understand compound words like bedroom and bookcase.","I can name the rooms and furniture in my home.","I can put two small words together to make a new word."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تسمية غرف البيت وأثاثه.","سيتمكن الطلاب من تكوين الكلمات المركبة مثل bedroom وbookcase وفهمها.","أستطيع أن أسمّي غرف بيتي وأثاثه.","أستطيع أن أجمع كلمتين صغيرتين لأكوّن كلمة جديدة."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"lamp","pos":"noun","ipa":"/læmp/","definition":"a thing that gives light","arabic":"مصباح","example":"Turn on the lamp, please.","image_id":"GV-L01-U5-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS3-W01"},{"word":"bookcase","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbʊkˌkeɪs/","definition":"a piece of furniture with shelves for books","arabic":"مكتبة (خزانة كتب)","example":"The bookcase is full of storybooks.","image_id":"GV-L01-U5-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS3-W02"},{"word":"rug","pos":"noun","ipa":"/rʌɡ/","definition":"a small carpet on the floor","arabic":"سجادة صغيرة","example":"The rug in the hall is red and gold.","image_id":"GV-L01-U5-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS3-W03"},{"word":"stairs","pos":"noun","ipa":"/stɛrz/","definition":"steps that go up or down in a building","arabic":"درج / سلالم","example":"Walk slowly on the stairs.","image_id":"GV-L01-U5-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS3-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"A compound word is two small words joined to make a new word: bed + room = bedroom. The two small words help you guess the meaning.\nSome compound words are one word (bookcase), and some are two words (living room).\nGroup house words by room: what is in the kitchen? what is in the bedroom?\nCollocations/phrases: bed + room = bedroom • bath + room = bathroom • book + case = bookcase • up + stairs = upstairs | two-word compounds: living room • dining room • washing machine | kitchen: oven, fridge, sink • bedroom: bed, lamp, wardrobe • living room: sofa, rug, TV","examples":["Our kitchen is small but clean.","The bathroom is at the end of the hall.","My little brother sleeps in my bedroom.","Put the books back in the bookcase.","The new sofa is very comfortable.","Grandma's rug has beautiful patterns.","The stairs go up to the roof.","We eat lunch in the dining room."],"common_errors":["✗ room bed → ✓ bedroom (In compound words, the \"kind\" word comes first: bed + room.)","✗ We cook in the bedroom. → ✓ We cook in the kitchen. (Use the correct room word.)","✗ The stair is long. → ✓ The stairs are long. (We usually say stairs (plural).)"],"arabic":"الكلمة المركبة تتكون من كلمتين: bed + room = bedroom (غرفة النوم).\nفي الإنجليزية تأتي كلمة النوع أولًا: bedroom وليس room bed.\nبعض الكلمات المركبة كلمتان منفصلتان: living room."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Rooms and Furniture: Compound Words”. Let’s learn rooms and furniture; compound words (bed + room = bedroom) together.","on_screen":"GV-L01-U5-LS3 | Rooms and Furniture: Compound Words","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. lamp: a thing that gives light. bookcase: a piece of furniture with shelves for books. rug: a small carpet on the floor.","on_screen":"lamp | bookcase | rug","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"A compound word is two small words joined to make a new word: bed + room = bedroom. The two small words help you guess the meaning. Some compound words are one word (bookcase), and some are two words (living room).","on_screen":"rooms and furniture; compound words (bed + room = bedroom)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Our kitchen is small but clean. The bathroom is at the end of the hall. My little brother sleeps in my bedroom.","on_screen":"Our kitchen is small but clean. / The bathroom is at the end of the hall. / My little brother sleeps in my bedroom.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “room bed.” That’s not right. We say: “bedroom.” In compound words, the \"kind\" word comes first: bed + room.","on_screen":"✗ room bed   ✓ bedroom","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: What do \"bed\" and \"room\" make together? … Think! … *bedroom* – a room with a bed. Great job! Now you can say: I can name the rooms and furniture in my home.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can name the rooms and furniture in my home.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: rooms and furniture; compound words (bed + room = bedroom).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","الكلمة المركبة تتكون من كلمتين: bed + room = bedroom (غرفة النوم).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: room bed — الصحيح: bedroom","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أسمّي غرف بيتي وأثاثه."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"bath + room = ___","options":["bathroom","bath room","bathsroom","roombath"],"answer":"bathroom","explanation":"Join the two small words: first word + second word.","explanation_ar":"اجمع الكلمتين."},{"q":"book + case = ___","options":["casebook","bookcase","books case","book cases"],"answer":"bookcase","explanation":"Join the two small words: first word + second word.","explanation_ar":"اجمع الكلمتين."},{"q":"We cook dinner in the ___.","options":["kitchen","bathroom","bedroom","garden"],"answer":"kitchen","explanation":"Think about what we do in each room.","explanation_ar":"فكّر فيما نفعله في كل غرفة."},{"q":"We sleep in the ___.","options":["kitchen","hall","bedroom","garden"],"answer":"bedroom","explanation":"Think about what we do in each room.","explanation_ar":"فكّر فيما نفعله في كل غرفة."},{"q":"We sit on the ___ and watch TV.","options":["oven","sofa","stairs","sink"],"answer":"sofa","explanation":"Think about where the furniture goes.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في مكان قطعة الأثاث."},{"q":"We go up the ___ to the second floor.","options":["lamp","bookcase","rug","stairs"],"answer":"stairs","explanation":"Think about where the furniture goes.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في مكان قطعة الأثاث."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the two halves to make compound words.","items":[{"q":"bed","options":["room","brush","paste","flower","case","stairs"],"answer":"room","explanation":"bed → room. Join the two small words: first word + second word.","explanation_ar":"اجمع الكلمتين."},{"q":"book","options":["room","brush","paste","flower","case","stairs"],"answer":"case","explanation":"book → case. Join the two small words: first word + second word.","explanation_ar":"اجمع الكلمتين."},{"q":"up","options":["room","brush","paste","flower","case","stairs"],"answer":"stairs","explanation":"up → stairs. Join the two small words: first word + second word.","explanation_ar":"اجمع الكلمتين."},{"q":"hair","options":["room","brush","paste","flower","case","stairs"],"answer":"brush","explanation":"hair → brush. Join the two small words: first word + second word.","explanation_ar":"اجمع الكلمتين."},{"q":"tooth","options":["room","brush","paste","flower","case","stairs"],"answer":"paste","explanation":"tooth → paste. Join the two small words: first word + second word.","explanation_ar":"اجمع الكلمتين."},{"q":"sun","options":["room","brush","paste","flower","case","stairs"],"answer":"flower","explanation":"sun → flower. Join the two small words: first word + second word.","explanation_ar":"اجمع الكلمتين."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write about the rooms in your home.","items":[{"q":"In our kitchen, there is a ___.","options":[],"answer":"In our kitchen, there is a big fridge.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses rooms and furniture; compound words (bed + room = bedroom) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"In my bedroom, there is a ___.","options":[],"answer":"In my bedroom, there is a wardrobe.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses rooms and furniture; compound words (bed + room = bedroom) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My favorite room is the ___.","options":[],"answer":"My favorite room is the living room.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses rooms and furniture; compound words (bed + room = bedroom) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"The bathroom is next to the ___.","options":[],"answer":"The bathroom is next to my bedroom.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses rooms and furniture; compound words (bed + room = bedroom) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Make a compound word with \"sun\": sun + ___ = ___","options":[],"answer":"sun + light = sunlight","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses rooms and furniture; compound words (bed + room = bedroom) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Design a room.","items":[{"q":"Draw your dream bedroom. Label 5 pieces of furniture.","options":[],"answer":"bed, lamp, rug, bookcase, desk","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses rooms and furniture; compound words (bed + room = bedroom) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 sentences about your dream room.","options":[],"answer":"There is a big bed. There is a bookcase next to the window. The rug is blue.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses rooms and furniture; compound words (bed + room = bedroom) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 compound words you know and draw them.","options":[],"answer":"football, sunflower, toothbrush","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses rooms and furniture; compound words (bed + room = bedroom) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Vocabulary Bingo","mechanic":"matching","rules":["Students write nine words from the list in their grid.","The teacher (or a student caller) reads a definition or Arabic meaning.","Students cross out the matching word.","Three in a row = \"Bingo!\" The winner must read the words and say what each means."],"data":[{"word":"house","match":"a building where a family lives","arabic":"بيت / منزل"},{"word":"kitchen","match":"the room where we cook food","arabic":"مطبخ"},{"word":"bedroom","match":"the room where we sleep","arabic":"غرفة نوم"},{"word":"bathroom","match":"the room where we wash","arabic":"دورة المياه / الحمّام"},{"word":"living room","match":"the room where the family sits and talks","arabic":"غرفة المعيشة"},{"word":"garden","match":"the land outside a house with plants and flowers","arabic":"حديقة"},{"word":"sofa","match":"a long soft seat for two or more people","arabic":"أريكة / كنبة"},{"word":"bed","match":"the thing you sleep on","arabic":"سرير"},{"word":"lamp","match":"a thing that gives light","arabic":"مصباح"},{"word":"bookcase","match":"a piece of furniture with shelves for books","arabic":"مكتبة (خزانة كتب)"},{"word":"rug","match":"a small carpet on the floor","arabic":"سجادة صغيرة"},{"word":"stairs","match":"steps that go up or down in a building","arabic":"درج / سلالم"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"up + stairs = ___","options":["up stair","upstair","upstairs","stairsup"],"answer":"upstairs","explanation":"Join the two small words: first word + second word.","explanation_ar":"اجمع الكلمتين."},{"q":"hair + brush = ___","options":["hair brushes","hairs brush","hairbrush","brushhair"],"answer":"hairbrush","explanation":"Join the two small words: first word + second word.","explanation_ar":"اجمع الكلمتين."},{"q":"We wash our hands in the ___.","options":["bedroom","bathroom","living room","garden"],"answer":"bathroom","explanation":"Think about what we do in each room.","explanation_ar":"فكّر فيما نفعله في كل غرفة."},{"q":"Mom keeps the food cold in the ___.","options":["fridge","lamp","sofa","bookcase"],"answer":"fridge","explanation":"Think about where the furniture goes.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في مكان قطعة الأثاث."},{"q":"There is a soft ___ on the floor.","options":["rug","sink","stairs","oven"],"answer":"rug","explanation":"Think about where the furniture goes.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في مكان قطعة الأثاث."},{"q":"A room with a bed is a ___.","options":["bathroom","kitchen","garden","bedroom"],"answer":"bedroom","explanation":"Join the two small words: first word + second word.","explanation_ar":"اجمع الكلمتين."},{"q":"We keep our books in a ___.","options":["bathtub","fridge","sink","bookcase"],"answer":"bookcase","explanation":"Think about where the furniture goes.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في مكان قطعة الأثاث."},{"q":"The family sits and talks in the ___.","options":["kitchen sink","living room","garage","bathroom"],"answer":"living room","explanation":"Think about what we do in each room.","explanation_ar":"فكّر فيما نفعله في كل غرفة."},{"q":"Which word is a compound word?","options":["sunflower","flower","garden","yellow"],"answer":"sunflower","explanation":"Join the two small words: first word + second word.","explanation_ar":"اجمع الكلمتين."},{"q":"Plants and flowers grow in the ___.","options":["bedroom","bathroom","garden","hall"],"answer":"garden","explanation":"Think about what we do in each room.","explanation_ar":"فكّر فيما نفعله في كل غرفة."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"A cut-away dollhouse showing a kitchen, bathroom, two bedrooms, a living room with a sofa and bookcase, and stairs, with Zaki joining word cards \"bed + room\". Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A cut-away dollhouse showing a kitchen, bathroom, two bedrooms, a living room with a sofa and bookcase, and stairs, with Zaki joining word cards \"bed + room\""},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 4 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 4 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows lamp (a thing that gives light); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing lamp: a thing that gives light"},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows bookcase (a piece of furniture with shelves for books); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing bookcase: a piece of furniture with shelves for books"},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows rug (a small carpet on the floor); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing rug: a small carpet on the floor"},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows stairs (steps that go up or down in a building); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing stairs: steps that go up or down in a building"},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Vocabulary Bingo”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Vocabulary Bingo"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS3-W01","script":"lamp. lamp. Turn on the lamp, please.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS3-W02","script":"bookcase. bookcase. The bookcase is full of storybooks.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS3-W03","script":"rug. rug. The rug in the hall is red and gold.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS3-W04","script":"stairs. stairs. Walk slowly on the stairs.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Rooms and Furniture: Compound Words”. Let’s learn rooms and furniture; compound words (bed + room = bedroom) together. Meet some new words. lamp: a thing that gives light. bookcase: a piece of furniture with shelves for books. rug: a small carpet on the floor. A compound word is two small words joined to make a new word: bed + room = bedroom. The two small words help you guess the meaning. Some compound words are one word (bookcase), and some are two words (living room). Here are some examples. Our kitchen is small but clean. The bathroom is at the end of the hall. My little brother sleeps in my bedroom. Be careful! Some learners say: “room bed.” That’s not right. We say: “bedroom.” In compound words, the \"kind\" word comes first: bed + room. Quick check: What do \"bed\" and \"room\" make together? … Think! … *bedroom* – a room with a bed. Great job! Now you can say: I can name the rooms and furniture in my home.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS4","title":"Sofas, Lamps, and Rugs: Commas in a List","objectives":["Students will be able to use commas to separate three or more things in a list.","Students will be able to write lists with and before the last item.","I can use commas in a list.","I can write \"a bed, a desk, and a lamp\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام الفاصلة للفصل بين ثلاثة أشياء أو أكثر في قائمة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة القوائم مع and قبل العنصر الأخير.","أستطيع أن أستخدم الفاصلة في القائمة.","أستطيع أن أكتب a bed, a desk, and a lamp."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"house","pos":"noun","ipa":"/haʊs/","definition":"a building where a family lives","arabic":"بيت / منزل","example":"Our house has a blue door.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"kitchen","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkɪtʃən/","definition":"the room where we cook food","arabic":"مطبخ","example":"Mom is making tea in the kitchen.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"bedroom","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbɛˌdrum/","definition":"the room where we sleep","arabic":"غرفة نوم","example":"My bedroom has a big window.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"bathroom","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbæˌθrum/","definition":"the room where we wash","arabic":"دورة المياه / الحمّام","example":"The bathroom is next to my room.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"living room","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈlɪvɪŋ rum/","definition":"the room where the family sits and talks","arabic":"غرفة المعيشة","example":"We watch the news in the living room.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"garden","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɡɑrdən/","definition":"the land outside a house with plants and flowers","arabic":"حديقة","example":"Grandpa waters the garden every evening.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"When we list three or more things, we put a comma (,) between them and and before the last thing: a bed, a desk, and a lamp.\nMany American schools put a comma before and in a list (a bed, a desk, and a lamp). We use this style in our books. Some writers leave it out – both can be correct, but be the same every time.\nWith only two things, use and with no comma: a sofa and a rug.\nThree or more things → commas between them: chairs, tables, and lamps\nPut and before the last thing.\nTwo things → no comma: a cat and a dog\nThe Arabic comma (،) looks different – in English use (,).","examples":["My room has a bed, a desk, and a lamp.","We have a cat, a parrot, and two fish.","The kitchen has an oven, a fridge, and a sink.","I like red, blue, and green.","There are sofas, rugs, and lamps in the shop.","Grandma grows mint, tomatoes, and lemons.","Omar, Yusuf, and Adam are cousins.","My bag and my coat are on the chair."],"common_errors":["✗ I have a pen a ruler and a book. → ✓ I have a pen, a ruler, and a book. (Put commas between things in a list.)","✗ a sofa, and a rug → ✓ a sofa and a rug (Two things → no comma.)","✗ milk، bread، and eggs → ✓ milk, bread, and eggs (Use the English comma (,).)"],"arabic":"نستخدم الفاصلة (,) بين ثلاثة أشياء أو أكثر في القائمة، ونضع and قبل الأخير.\nإذا كان هناك شيئان فقط نستخدم and بدون فاصلة: a sofa and a rug.\nانتبه: الفاصلة الإنجليزية (,) تختلف عن العربية (،)."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Sofas, Lamps, and Rugs: Commas in a List”. Let’s learn commas in a list (series) together.","on_screen":"GV-L01-U5-LS4 | Sofas, Lamps, and Rugs: Commas in a List","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"When we list three or more things, we put a comma (,) between them and and before the last thing: a bed, a desk, and a lamp.","on_screen":"commas in a list (series)","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"When we list three or more things, we put a comma (,) between them and and before the last thing: a bed, a desk, and a lamp. Many American schools put a comma before and in a list (a bed, a desk, and a lamp). We use this style in our books. Some writers leave it out – both can be correct, but be the same every time.","on_screen":"Three or more things → commas between them: chairs, tables, and lamps • Put and before the last thing. • Two things → no comma: a cat and a dog","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. My room has a bed, a desk, and a lamp. We have a cat, a parrot, and two fish. The kitchen has an oven, a fridge, and a sink.","on_screen":"My room has a bed, a desk, and a lamp. / We have a cat, a parrot, and two fish. / The kitchen has an oven, a fridge, and a sink.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I have a pen a ruler and a book.” That’s not right. We say: “I have a pen, a ruler, and a book.” Put commas between things in a list.","on_screen":"✗ I have a pen a ruler and a book.   ✓ I have a pen, a ruler, and a book.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: How many things do we need before we use commas in a list? … Think! … Three or more. Great job! Now you can say: I can use commas in a list.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can use commas in a list.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: commas in a list (series).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نستخدم الفاصلة (,) بين ثلاثة أشياء أو أكثر في القائمة، ونضع and قبل الأخير.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I have a pen a ruler and a book. — الصحيح: I have a pen, a ruler, and a book.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أستخدم الفاصلة في القائمة."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Shopping for My Room (editing passage)","body":"Today Dad and I go shopping. We buy a lamp a rug and a bookcase. Mom buys cups plates, and spoons. My sister buys a pillow, and a blanket. We are tired hungry, and happy!","word_count":35,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct sentence.","items":[{"q":"","options":["We need eggs, milk, and bread.","We need, eggs milk and bread.","We need eggs milk and bread.","We need eggs, milk, bread. and"],"answer":"We need eggs, milk, and bread.","explanation":"Three or more things → commas between them and and before the last.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة أشياء أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"","options":["I have, a cat and a dog.","I have a cat, and a dog.","I have a cat and a dog.","I have a cat a dog."],"answer":"I have a cat and a dog.","explanation":"Two things → and, no comma.","explanation_ar":"شيئان ← and بدون فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["The garden has roses mint and palm trees.","The garden has roses, mint, and palm trees.","The garden has roses, mint, palm and trees.","The garden has, roses, mint and palm trees."],"answer":"The garden has roses, mint, and palm trees.","explanation":"Three or more things → commas between them and and before the last.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة أشياء أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"","options":["Lina Sara, and Noura are friends.","Lina, Sara, and Noura are friends.","Lina Sara and Noura are friends.","Lina, Sara, and, Noura are friends."],"answer":"Lina, Sara, and Noura are friends.","explanation":"Three or more things → commas between them and and before the last.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة أشياء أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"","options":["My room has a bed a lamp and a rug.","My room has a bed، a lamp، and a rug.","My room has, a bed a lamp, a rug.","My room has a bed, a lamp, and a rug."],"answer":"My room has a bed, a lamp, and a rug.","explanation":"Use the English comma (,).","explanation_ar":"استخدم الفاصلة الإنجليزية."},{"q":"","options":["We have, a sofa and a TV.","We have a sofa, and a TV.","We have a sofa a TV.","We have a sofa and a TV."],"answer":"We have a sofa and a TV.","explanation":"Two things → and, no comma.","explanation_ar":"شيئان ← and بدون فاصلة."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS4-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Add the missing commas.","items":[{"q":"I see a bed a desk, and a chair.","options":[],"answer":"I see a bed, a desk, and a chair.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Three or more things → commas between them and and before the last.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. ثلاثة أشياء أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"Our kitchen has cups, plates and bowls.","options":[],"answer":"Our kitchen has cups, plates, and bowls.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Three or more things → commas between them and and before the last.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. ثلاثة أشياء أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"Ali Fahad, and Saad play football.","options":[],"answer":"Ali, Fahad, and Saad play football.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Three or more things → commas between them and and before the last.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. ثلاثة أشياء أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"I like apples, grapes and dates.","options":[],"answer":"I like apples, grapes, and dates.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Three or more things → commas between them and and before the last.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. ثلاثة أشياء أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"There are lamps rugs, and mirrors in the hall.","options":[],"answer":"There are lamps, rugs, and mirrors in the hall.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Three or more things → commas between them and and before the last.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. ثلاثة أشياء أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"My cousin has a horse, and a camel.","options":[],"answer":"My cousin has a horse and a camel.","explanation":", → (delete). Two things → and, no comma.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: , → (delete). شيئان ← and بدون فاصلة."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the shopping list paragraph.","items":[{"q":"We buy a lamp a rug and a bookcase.","options":[],"answer":"We buy a lamp, a rug, and a bookcase.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Three or more things → commas between them and and before the last.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. ثلاثة أشياء أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"We buy a lamp a rug and a bookcase.","options":[],"answer":"We buy a lamp, a rug, and a bookcase.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Three or more things → commas between them and and before the last.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. ثلاثة أشياء أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"We buy a lamp a rug and a bookcase.","options":[],"answer":"We buy a lamp, a rug, and a bookcase.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Three or more things → commas between them and and before the last.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. ثلاثة أشياء أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"My sister buys a pillow, and a blanket.","options":[],"answer":"My sister buys a pillow and a blanket.","explanation":", → (delete). Three or more things → commas between them and and before the last.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: , → (delete). ثلاثة أشياء أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"We buy a lamp a rug and a bookcase.","options":[],"answer":"We buy a lamp, a rug, and a bookcase.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Three or more things → commas between them and and before the last.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. ثلاثة أشياء أو أكثر ← فواصل."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write lists.","items":[{"q":"Write a list of 3 things in your kitchen with commas.","options":[],"answer":"Our kitchen has a fridge, an oven, and a sink.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses commas in a list (series) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write the names of 3 friends in one sentence.","options":[],"answer":"Saad, Fahad, and Turki are my friends.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses commas in a list (series) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with only two things (no comma!).","options":[],"answer":"I have a bike and a ball.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses commas in a list (series) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Letter Ladder","mechanic":"word_builder","rules":["The leader chooses a word from the list and draws one blank line per letter.","Teams take turns guessing letters. Correct letters are written on the lines.","Each wrong guess removes one rung of the ladder (start with 6 rungs).","The team that completes the word scores 2 points and uses it in a sentence."],"data":[{"word":"kitchen","clue":"the room where we cook food"},{"word":"bedroom","clue":"the room where we sleep"},{"word":"bathroom","clue":"the room where we wash"},{"word":"garden","clue":"the land outside a house with plants and flowers"},{"word":"sofa","clue":"a long soft seat for two or more people"},{"word":"lamp","clue":"a thing that gives light"},{"word":"house","clue":"a building where a family lives"},{"word":"bed","clue":"the thing you sleep on"},{"word":"bookcase","clue":"a piece of furniture with shelves for books"},{"word":"rug","clue":"a small carpet on the floor"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"","options":["We have tea, juice, and water.","We have tea juice and water.","We have, tea, juice and water.","We have tea, juice, water and."],"answer":"We have tea, juice, and water.","explanation":"Three or more things → commas between them and and before the last.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة أشياء أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"Where does the comma go? \"I need a pen ___ a ruler, and a notebook.\"","options":["after ruler","after pen","after need","after a"],"answer":"after pen","explanation":"Three or more things → commas between them and and before the last.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة أشياء أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"","options":["My, bag and my shoes are here.","My bag and my shoes are here.","My bag, and my shoes are here.","My bag, my shoes, are here."],"answer":"My bag and my shoes are here.","explanation":"Two things → and, no comma.","explanation_ar":"شيئان ← and بدون فاصلة."},{"q":"How many commas? \"We have a sofa a rug and a lamp.\"","options":["1","3","2","0"],"answer":"2","explanation":"Three or more things → commas between them and and before the last.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة أشياء أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"","options":["I like cats, rabbits, and birds.","I like cats، rabbits، and birds.","I like, cats rabbits, and birds.","I like cats rabbits and birds."],"answer":"I like cats, rabbits, and birds.","explanation":"Use the English comma (,).","explanation_ar":"استخدم الفاصلة الإنجليزية."},{"q":"","options":["Mom, Dad, and Grandma are in the garden.","Mom, Dad, Grandma and, are in the garden.","Mom Dad and Grandma are in the garden.","Mom Dad, and Grandma are in the garden."],"answer":"Mom, Dad, and Grandma are in the garden.","explanation":"Three or more things → commas between them and and before the last.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة أشياء أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"Which list has two things only?","options":["chairs, tables, and lamps","a chair, a table, and a lamp","a rug, a bed, and a sofa","a chair and a table"],"answer":"a chair and a table","explanation":"Two things → and, no comma.","explanation_ar":"شيئان ← and بدون فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["The house has a kitchen two bathrooms and four bedrooms.","The house has a kitchen, two bathrooms, and four bedrooms.","The house has, a kitchen, two bathrooms and four bedrooms.","The house has a kitchen, two bathrooms, four bedrooms and."],"answer":"The house has a kitchen, two bathrooms, and four bedrooms.","explanation":"Three or more things → commas between them and and before the last.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة أشياء أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"Which comma is the English comma?","options":[".","،",",",";"],"answer":",","explanation":"Use the English comma (,).","explanation_ar":"استخدم الفاصلة الإنجليزية."},{"q":"","options":["I see a bird a cat, and a dog.","I see, a bird, a cat and a dog","I see a bird, a cat, and, a dog.","I see a bird, a cat, and a dog."],"answer":"I see a bird, a cat, and a dog.","explanation":"Three or more things → commas between them and and before the last.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة أشياء أو أكثر ← فواصل."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “My Home” that shows commas in a list (series) in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “My Home” that shows commas in a list (series) in action"},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Letter Ladder”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Letter Ladder"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Sofas, Lamps, and Rugs: Commas in a List”. Let’s learn commas in a list (series) together. When we list three or more things, we put a comma (,) between them and and before the last thing: a bed, a desk, and a lamp. When we list three or more things, we put a comma (,) between them and and before the last thing: a bed, a desk, and a lamp. Many American schools put a comma before and in a list (a bed, a desk, and a lamp). We use this style in our books. Some writers leave it out – both can be correct, but be the same every time. Here are some examples. My room has a bed, a desk, and a lamp. We have a cat, a parrot, and two fish. The kitchen has an oven, a fridge, and a sink. Be careful! Some learners say: “I have a pen a ruler and a book.” That’s not right. We say: “I have a pen, a ruler, and a book.” Put commas between things in a list. Quick check: How many things do we need before we use commas in a list? … Think! … Three or more. Great job! Now you can say: I can use commas in a list.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS5","title":"My Dream House: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to describe a house using there is/are and prepositions of place.","Students will be able to write a description of a dream house with commas in lists.","I can describe a house and say where things are.","I can write about my dream house."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من وصف بيت باستخدام there is/are وحروف الجر.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة وصف لبيت أحلامهم مع الفواصل في القوائم.","أستطيع أن أصف بيتًا وأقول أين توجد الأشياء.","أستطيع أن أكتب عن بيت أحلامي."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"house","pos":"noun","ipa":"/haʊs/","definition":"a building where a family lives","arabic":"بيت / منزل","example":"Our house has a blue door.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"kitchen","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkɪtʃən/","definition":"the room where we cook food","arabic":"مطبخ","example":"Mom is making tea in the kitchen.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"bedroom","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbɛˌdrum/","definition":"the room where we sleep","arabic":"غرفة نوم","example":"My bedroom has a big window.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"bathroom","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbæˌθrum/","definition":"the room where we wash","arabic":"دورة المياه / الحمّام","example":"The bathroom is next to my room.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"living room","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈlɪvɪŋ rum/","definition":"the room where the family sits and talks","arabic":"غرفة المعيشة","example":"We watch the news in the living room.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"garden","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɡɑrdən/","definition":"the land outside a house with plants and flowers","arabic":"حديقة","example":"Grandpa waters the garden every evening.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"sofa","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsoʊfə/","definition":"a long soft seat for two or more people","arabic":"أريكة / كنبة","example":"The cat is asleep on the sofa.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"bed","pos":"noun","ipa":"/bɛd/","definition":"the thing you sleep on","arabic":"سرير","example":"Make your bed in the morning.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"lamp","pos":"noun","ipa":"/læmp/","definition":"a thing that gives light","arabic":"مصباح","example":"Turn on the lamp, please.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"bookcase","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbʊkˌkeɪs/","definition":"a piece of furniture with shelves for books","arabic":"مكتبة (خزانة كتب)","example":"The bookcase is full of storybooks.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"rug","pos":"noun","ipa":"/rʌɡ/","definition":"a small carpet on the floor","arabic":"سجادة صغيرة","example":"The rug in the hall is red and gold.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"stairs","pos":"noun","ipa":"/stɛrz/","definition":"steps that go up or down in a building","arabic":"درج / سلالم","example":"Walk slowly on the stairs.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 5: there is / there are, prepositions of place, house words and commas in lists.\nA good description takes the reader from room to room and says where things are.\n✔ There is + one thing / There are + many things\n✔ in, on, under, next to, behind, in front of\n✔ commas in a list of three or more","examples":["There is a pool behind the house.","There are three bathrooms.","The bookcase is next to the window.","My dream kitchen has a big oven, a fridge, and an island.","Is there a garden? – Yes, there is.","There are no stairs in our flat.","A big palm tree is in front of the door.","There's a balcony on the top floor."],"common_errors":["✗ There is a pool and there is a garden and there is a gym. → ✓ There is a pool, a garden, and a gym. (Use a list with commas.)","✗ The lamp is next the sofa. → ✓ The lamp is next to the sofa. (next to.)","✗ In my dream house have a cinema. → ✓ There is a cinema in my dream house. (Use there is.)"],"arabic":"نراجع there is/are وحروف الجر وكلمات البيت والفواصل في القوائم.\nبدلًا من تكرار there is كثيرًا، اجمع الأشياء في قائمة بفواصل.\nالوصف الجيد يتنقل من غرفة إلى غرفة ويحدد مكان الأشياء."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “My Dream House: Language in Use”. Let’s learn there is/are, prepositions, house words and commas in lists (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L01-U5-LS5 | My Dream House: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Picture difference: Partner A describes a room picture (\"There is a lamp next to the sofa\"); Partner B finds five differences in his/her picture.","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 5: there is / there are, prepositions of place, house words and commas in lists. A good description takes the reader from room to room and says where things are.","on_screen":"✔ There is + one thing / There are + many things • ✔ in, on, under, next to, behind, in front of • ✔ commas in a list of three or more","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. There is a pool behind the house. There are three bathrooms. The bookcase is next to the window.","on_screen":"There is a pool behind the house. / There are three bathrooms. / The bookcase is next to the window.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “There is a pool and there is a garden and there is a gym.” That’s not right. We say: “There is a pool, a garden, and a gym.” Use a list with commas.","on_screen":"✗ There is a pool and there is a garden and there is a gym.   ✓ There is a pool, a garden, and a gym.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “The lamp is next the sofa.”? … Think! … It should be “The lamp is next to the sofa.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can describe a house and say where things are.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can describe a house and say where things are.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: there is/are, prepositions, house words and commas in lists (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع there is/are وحروف الجر وكلمات البيت والفواصل في القوائم.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: There is a pool and there is a garden and there is a gym. — الصحيح: There is a pool, a garden, and a gym.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أصف بيتًا وأقول أين توجد الأشياء."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"My Dream House – Sara","body":"My dream house is big and bright. There are five bedrooms upstairs.\nThere is a reading room with a sofa, a lamp, and many bookcases.\nThere is a garden behind the house. There are flowers, palm trees, and a small pool in it.\nMy bedroom is next to the reading room.\nI love my dream house!","word_count":56,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Sara's text. True or False?","items":[{"q":"Sara's dream house has five bedrooms.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “My Dream House – Sara”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The reading room has a TV.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “My Dream House – Sara”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The garden is in front of the house.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “My Dream House – Sara”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"There is a small pool in the garden.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “My Dream House – Sara”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Sara's bedroom is next to the reading room.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “My Dream House – Sara”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The bedrooms are downstairs.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “My Dream House – Sara”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"There ___ a fountain in the garden.","options":["have","is","are","am"],"answer":"is","explanation":"one thing → there is; many → there are.","explanation_ar":"المفرد there is والجمع there are."},{"q":"The cat sleeps ___ the sofa. (below)","options":["of","on","under","in"],"answer":"under","explanation":"Choose the preposition that shows the right place.","explanation_ar":"اختر حرف الجر المناسب للمكان."},{"q":"We wash the dishes in the kitchen ___.","options":["sink","sofa","stairs","rug"],"answer":"sink","explanation":"Choose the right house word.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة البيت الصحيحة."},{"q":"","options":["Our garden has, roses lemons, mint.","Our garden has roses، lemons، and mint.","Our garden has roses lemons and mint.","Our garden has roses, lemons, and mint."],"answer":"Our garden has roses, lemons, and mint.","explanation":"Three or more things → commas.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة أشياء أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"","options":["Where is the bathroom?","Where the bathroom is?","Where is the bathroom.","where is the bathroom?"],"answer":"Where is the bathroom?","explanation":"Start with a capital letter; end with the right mark.","explanation_ar":"ابدأ بحرف كبير وأنهِ بالعلامة المناسبة."},{"q":"There ___ two balconies.","options":["is","has","are","am"],"answer":"are","explanation":"one thing → there is; many → there are.","explanation_ar":"المفرد there is والجمع there are."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Picture difference. Write the differences.","items":[{"q":"In my picture, the lamp is ___ the sofa.","options":[],"answer":"In my picture, the lamp is next to the sofa.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses there is/are, prepositions, house words and commas in lists (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"In your picture, there ___ two cushions.","options":[],"answer":"In your picture, there are two cushions.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses there is/are, prepositions, house words and commas in lists (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"In my picture, the cat is ___ the table.","options":[],"answer":"In my picture, the cat is under the table.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses there is/are, prepositions, house words and commas in lists (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"In your picture, there isn't a ___.","options":[],"answer":"In your picture, there isn't a clock.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses there is/are, prepositions, house words and commas in lists (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"In my picture, there are books, ___, and ___ on the shelf.","options":[],"answer":"In my picture, there are books, toys, and a plant on the shelf.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses there is/are, prepositions, house words and commas in lists (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write about your dream house.","items":[{"q":"Plan: list the rooms and 3 special things.","options":[],"answer":"6 bedrooms; game room; garden with a pool, swings, and trees","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses there is/are, prepositions, house words and commas in lists (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 5–6 sentences about your dream house.","options":[],"answer":"My dream house is near the sea. There are six bedrooms. There is a game room next to the kitchen. The garden has a pool, swings, and trees. I love it!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses there is/are, prepositions, house words and commas in lists (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: is/are? prepositions? commas? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"There is six bedrooms\" to \"There are six bedrooms\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses there is/are, prepositions, house words and commas in lists (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Treasure Hunt Review","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["Teams move to a station every 90 seconds.","At each station, write one correct sentence with the cue word and there is/are, prepositions, house words and commas in lists (unit review).","Teams collect a \"treasure letter\" for each correct sentence.","Unscramble the letters at the end to reveal the secret word."],"data":[{"cue":"house","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"kitchen","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"bedroom","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"bathroom","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"living room","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"garden","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"sofa","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"bed","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"lamp","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"bookcase","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"rug","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"stairs","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"There ___ a big mirror in the hall.","options":["is","are","have","am"],"answer":"is","explanation":"one thing → there is; many → there are.","explanation_ar":"المفرد there is والجمع there are."},{"q":"There ___ many cushions on the sofa.","options":["has","am","is","are"],"answer":"are","explanation":"one thing → there is; many → there are.","explanation_ar":"المفرد there is والجمع there are."},{"q":"The car is ___ the garage. (inside)","options":["in","next","on","under"],"answer":"in","explanation":"Choose the preposition that shows the right place.","explanation_ar":"اختر حرف الجر المناسب للمكان."},{"q":"The painting is ___ the wall.","options":["at of","under","on","in"],"answer":"on","explanation":"Choose the preposition that shows the right place.","explanation_ar":"اختر حرف الجر المناسب للمكان."},{"q":"We keep clothes in a ___.","options":["fridge","oven","wardrobe","sink"],"answer":"wardrobe","explanation":"Choose the right house word.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة البيت الصحيحة."},{"q":"","options":["We need, chairs, tables and lamps.","We need chairs, tables, and lamps.","We need chairs tables and lamps.","We need chairs، tables، and lamps."],"answer":"We need chairs, tables, and lamps.","explanation":"Three or more things → commas.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة أشياء أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"","options":["Are there a garden behind your house?","Is there a garden behind your house.","There is a garden behind your house?","Is there a garden behind your house?"],"answer":"Is there a garden behind your house?","explanation":"one thing → there is; many → there are.","explanation_ar":"المفرد there is والجمع there are."},{"q":"The swing is ___ the house. (at the back)","options":["on","behind","in front","in of"],"answer":"behind","explanation":"Choose the preposition that shows the right place.","explanation_ar":"اختر حرف الجر المناسب للمكان."},{"q":"","options":["The kitchen next to is the living room.","The kitchen is next of the living room.","The kitchen is next to the living room.","The kitchen is next the living room."],"answer":"The kitchen is next to the living room.","explanation":"Choose the preposition that shows the right place.","explanation_ar":"اختر حرف الجر المناسب للمكان."},{"q":"Choose the best sentence for a house description:","options":["There is a pool, a garden, and a playroom.","There is a pool there is a garden there is a playroom.","There are pool, garden, playroom.","There is pool garden and playroom."],"answer":"There is a pool, a garden, and a playroom.","explanation":"Three or more things → commas.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة أشياء أو أكثر ← فواصل."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"Sara showing a colorful drawing of her dream house with a pool, a garden, a reading room full of books and a balcony. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Sara showing a colorful drawing of her dream house with a pool, a garden, a reading room full of books and a balcony"},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “My Home”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “My Home”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L01-U5-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Treasure Hunt Review”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Treasure Hunt Review"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS5-T1","script":"My dream house is big and bright. There are five bedrooms upstairs. There is a reading room with a sofa, a lamp, and many bookcases. There is a garden behind the house. There are flowers, palm trees, and a small pool in it. My bedroom is next to the reading room. I love my dream house!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U5-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “My Dream House: Language in Use”. Let’s learn there is/are, prepositions, house words and commas in lists (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Picture difference: Partner A describes a room picture (\"There is a lamp next to the sofa\"); Partner B finds five differences in his/her picture. Today you use all of Unit 5: there is / there are, prepositions of place, house words and commas in lists. A good description takes the reader from room to room and says where things are. Here are some examples. There is a pool behind the house. There are three bathrooms. The bookcase is next to the window. Be careful! Some learners say: “There is a pool and there is a garden and there is a gym.” That’s not right. We say: “There is a pool, a garden, and a gym.” Use a list with commas. Quick check: what is wrong with “The lamp is next the sofa.”? … Think! … It should be “The lamp is next to the sofa.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can describe a house and say where things are.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"___ a lamp on my desk.","options":["Is there","It have","There are","There is"],"answer":"There is","explanation":"One thing → there is.","explanation_ar":"للمفرد نستخدم there is."},{"q":"There ___ four chairs in the kitchen.","options":["are","is","am","has"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Two or more things → there are.","explanation_ar":"للجمع نستخدم there are."},{"q":"","options":["There is three bedrooms.","There are three bedroom.","There are three bedrooms.","It have three bedrooms."],"answer":"There are three bedrooms.","explanation":"Two or more things → there are.","explanation_ar":"للجمع نستخدم there are."},{"q":"","options":["There is a garden in my house.","There are a garden in my house.","In my house have a garden.","There is garden in my house."],"answer":"There is a garden in my house.","explanation":"Use there is/are, not have, to say something is in a place.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم there is وليس have."},{"q":"There ___ a washing machine in the bathroom.","options":["is","am","are","have"],"answer":"is","explanation":"One thing → there is.","explanation_ar":"للمفرد نستخدم there is."},{"q":"The ball is ___ the bed. (below)","options":["in","of","on","under"],"answer":"under","explanation":"under = below something.","explanation_ar":"under تعني تحت."},{"q":"The picture is ___ the wall.","options":["at of","on","in","under"],"answer":"on","explanation":"on = touching the top or a surface (a wall, a table).","explanation_ar":"on تعني على السطح."},{"q":"","options":["The school bus is in the front gate.","The school bus is in front of the gate.","The school bus is front of the gate.","The school bus is in front the gate."],"answer":"The school bus is in front of the gate.","explanation":"in front of = before; don't forget of.","explanation_ar":"in front of تعني أمام."},{"q":"___ any cookies in the jar?","options":["Are there","Is there","There are","There is"],"answer":"Are there","explanation":"Questions: Is there (one) / Are there any (many).","explanation_ar":"السؤال: Is there للمفرد وAre there any للجمع."},{"q":"The bag is ___ the door. (at the back)","options":["on","of","behind","in front"],"answer":"behind","explanation":"behind = at the back of.","explanation_ar":"behind تعني خلف."},{"q":"bed + room = ___","options":["bed room","roombed","beds room","bedroom"],"answer":"bedroom","explanation":"Join the two small words: first word + second word.","explanation_ar":"اجمع الكلمتين."},{"q":"We cook in the ___.","options":["bedroom","kitchen","garden","living room"],"answer":"kitchen","explanation":"Think about what we do in each room.","explanation_ar":"فكّر فيما نفعله في كل غرفة."},{"q":"We sit on the ___ in the living room.","options":["sofa","stairs","oven","sink"],"answer":"sofa","explanation":"Think about where the furniture goes.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في مكان قطعة الأثاث."},{"q":"Find the compound word.","options":["table","bookcase","rug","lamp"],"answer":"bookcase","explanation":"Join the two small words: first word + second word.","explanation_ar":"اجمع الكلمتين."},{"q":"We go down the ___ to the ground floor.","options":["rug","lamp","sofa","stairs"],"answer":"stairs","explanation":"Think about where the furniture goes.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في مكان قطعة الأثاث."},{"q":"A small carpet on the floor is a ___.","options":["sink","bed","lamp","rug"],"answer":"rug","explanation":"Think about where the furniture goes.","explanation_ar":"فكّر في مكان قطعة الأثاث."},{"q":"","options":["We need cups, plates, spoons and.","We need, cups, plates and spoons.","We need cups, plates, and spoons.","We need cups plates and spoons."],"answer":"We need cups, plates, and spoons.","explanation":"Three or more things → commas between them and and before the last.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة أشياء أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"","options":["I have a bike and a ball.","I have a bike, and a ball.","I have a bike a ball.","I have, a bike and a ball."],"answer":"I have a bike and a ball.","explanation":"Two things → and, no comma.","explanation_ar":"شيئان ← and بدون فاصلة."},{"q":"How many commas? \"We visit Abha Taif and Jeddah.\"","options":["0","2","1","3"],"answer":"2","explanation":"Three or more things → commas between them and and before the last.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة أشياء أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"Which comma is used in English?","options":[":","،",";",","],"answer":",","explanation":"Use the English comma (,).","explanation_ar":"استخدم الفاصلة الإنجليزية."},{"q":"","options":["Hamad, Rakan, and, Ziyad are brothers.","Hamad Rakan, and Ziyad are brothers.","Hamad, Rakan, and Ziyad are brothers.","Hamad Rakan and Ziyad are brothers."],"answer":"Hamad, Rakan, and Ziyad are brothers.","explanation":"Three or more things → commas between them and and before the last.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة أشياء أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"Choose the best sentence for \"My Home\":","options":["In our living room have a sofa.","There is a sofa, a TV, and a rug in our living room.","There is a sofa there is a TV there is a rug.","There are sofa TV rug."],"answer":"There is a sofa, a TV, and a rug in our living room.","explanation":"Three or more things → commas between them and and before the last.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة أشياء أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"there is two sofas in the room.\"","options":["there are two sofas in the room.","There is two sofas in the room.","There are two sofas in the room.","There are two sofa in the room."],"answer":"There are two sofas in the room.","explanation":"Two or more things → there are.","explanation_ar":"للجمع نستخدم there are."},{"q":"Where is the cat? – ___","options":["It behind the curtain.","There behind the curtain.","It's behind the curtain.","Is behind the curtain."],"answer":"It's behind the curtain.","explanation":"behind = at the back of.","explanation_ar":"behind تعني خلف."}],"theme_ar":"بيتي","essential_question_ar":"ما الذي يجعل البيت مكانًا دافئًا نحبه؟","can_do":"I can describe my home with there is / there are and say where things are with prepositions.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أصف بيتي باستخدام there is / there are وأقول أين توجد الأشياء باستخدام حروف الجر."});
